# React components — CNP Department

## Stack constraints

- React **functional components** only; TypeScript for all new code under `frontend/src/`.
- Routing, auth, and API access stay on existing paths: `App.tsx`, `AuthContext`, `services/api.ts`, `ProtectedRoute` / `RoleProtectedRoute`.
- Do not introduce alternate data layers (React Query, Redux, etc.) without explicit approval.

## Structure

- **One clear responsibility** per component (display vs form vs list item).
- Extract hooks (e.g. `useStudentDashboardData`) when a page mixes fetching, normalization, and layout—keep JSX readable.
- Prefer composition over prop drilling more than two levels; use context only when already established (`useAuth`).

## Types and props

- Explicit props interfaces; export types when reused.
- Reuse `User`, `Club`, `Project` from `types/index.ts`; extend locally only for populated API shapes.
- Avoid new `any`; narrow API responses with typed generics on `api<T>()`.

## Data and honesty

- Fetch via `api()`; handle `ApiError` messages for user-visible errors.
- Implement **loading, error, empty, and populated** states—no silent failures.
- Never render hard-coded lists, counts, or activity feeds as if they were API-backed.
- Do not add mock endpoints or fake `setTimeout` demo data in production pages.

## Reuse

- Reuse `UserDisplay`, `EventCard`, `StudentClubCard`, `StudentProjectCard`, button/badge classes before cloning markup.
- Do not replace working components for stylistic churn; refactor when it reduces duplication or fixes bugs.

## Side effects

- `useEffect` dependencies must include values used inside; avoid stale `user` in fetchers.
- Cancel or ignore stale responses when switching routes/users if race conditions appear.

## Files and routing

- New role dashboards: prefer dedicated page modules (e.g. `pages/Dashboard/StudentDashboard.tsx`) composed into `Dashboard.tsx` or routed separately—without breaking existing role branches until migration is intentional.
- Preserve `NAVIGATION` in `Sidebar.tsx` role filters when adding links.
